## 8. Success Criteria

The initial GitHub/CI milestone will be considered successful when:

- [ ] `main` is protected according to the agreed repository policy.
- [ ] Developers can work through feature branches and pull requests.
- [ ] Required CI checks run automatically and report their results.
- [ ] Security-check availability and enforcement rules are documented.
- [ ] Existing manual deployments remain usable while the new process is validated.
- [ ] The team has a documented next step for development and staging automation.

The later deployment milestone will be successful when:

- [ ] Application deployment is repeatable through GitHub Actions.
- [ ] Staging deployments require the agreed approval.
- [ ] Deployment verification and failure handling are documented and tested.
- [ ] Secrets are accessed securely and are not exposed in logs.
- [ ] Development and staging behavior is validated before production planning is finalized.

